	(gr_text_box "Notes:\n- Board stackup: 2-layer PCB, 35 µm copper, dielectric height 1.55 mm\n- The Antenna treace is designed for 50 Ω impedance → trace width = 2.88 mm\n- The USB 2.0 differential pair is designed for 90 Ω differential impedance → trace width = 1.26 mm, gap = 0.28 mm\n\nLimitations due to 2-Layer desing:\n- Due to the 2-layer constraint, a fully continuous ground plane is not possible.\n- USB differential pair does not have an uninterrupted ground reference along the entire path. I believe the layout is acceptable for usb 2.0 speeds, but am unsure\n- There are breaks in the ground plane near power routing and switching converters. This is unavoidable due to routing constraints and small IC package sizes.\n\nQuestions:\n- I am unsure if the antenna trace is implemented correctly. Specifically regarding trace necking into the IC pin and placement of ground stitching vias?\n- Is the USB routing acceptable given the ground plane interruptions?\n"
		(start 17.125 15.125)
		(end 278.375 61.375)
		(margins 1.0025 1.0025 1.0025 1.0025)
